# Jev adapter

Use `@typesafe-ai/sdk` as installed. Before calling it, read `node_modules/@typesafe-ai/sdk` types or https://docs.typesafe.ai. The project notes are `.cursor/context/jev.md`. If a note and the installed types disagree, the types win and the note is corrected.

Allowed questions are the SDK primitives: `choice`, `score`, and `noul`, sent through `TypeSafeClient.systemOne`. Do not add methods, fields, or response shapes the installed types do not declare.

The adapter maps answers into `IncidentDecision` and returns. It does not apply policy and does not perform an action.

Pin the model id used for a recorded decision. `jev-latest` may change. Store the id on the decision record.

If the SDK is not installed, stop. Do not stub a fictional client in production code.
